      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T12:26:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that we are moving away from using loop device for APEXes. APEXes will be activated by directly mounting from *.apex files, bypassing the need for loop devices.\n\nSo, I don\u0027t think we want to do this optimization for 16-qpr2 and later releases.\n\ncc: @jooyung@google.com",
      "revId": "1e903d3d5368db64fe1a2647c970a7cbc73fa3e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "967c0a74_93b7bdfc",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4656873
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T16:39:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Acknowledged. Thank you for the clarification. \nHowever, since our current project is based on Android 14 (specifically the android-automotiveos-14.0.0_lts5 tag) from our vendor chipset, we are still considering a backport of this optimization to improve performance on our current platform.\nIf it is allowed, could you advise on the best branch to target for this? We noticed android14-qpr1-automotiveos-release on Google Source, but we want to ensure we align with the proper maintenance path for Automotive A14. Should we target that branch, or is there a specific A14 main release branch you recommend?\n\nRegards,",
      "parentUuid": "b88fbacc_ef8f109b",
      "revId": "1e903d3d5368db64fe1a2647c970a7cbc73fa3e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e62655e6_4c74d334",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
